-- title:
--   Finite face-regularity states and one-cut refinement
-- statement:
--   A Boolean cut test is represented by its finite support and evaluated by its zero–one indicator. A real function is measurable with respect to a finite partition when it is constant on each atom.
--
--   A face-regularity state records the current partition. Its structured component is the conditional mean, its residual is the original function minus that component, and its energy is the mean square of the structured component. Boolean cut correlation is the normalized pairing of the residual with a cut indicator. Refinement by one cut joins the current partition with the partition generated by that cut's membership bit. Included support gives the finite energy-increment framework used by subsequent refinement definitions.
